items.prose:
A position book in £ holds one `Position` per symbol (hidden above your code):

```cpp
struct Position { std::string sym; int qty; double cash; };
struct Fill { std::string sym; int qty; double px; };
```

For each fill, find the position with the same symbol. Add the fill's quantity, and take `qty * px` from its cash. A sale has negative `qty`, so cash rises. An unknown symbol gets a new position at the end of the book.

